    {
      "title": "FinMin examining suggestions for changes in equity capital gains tax: CBDT",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/markets/news/finmin-examining-suggestions-for-changes-in-equity-capital-gains-tax-cbdt-126111601256_1.html",
      "description": "The Finance Ministry is examining various aspects of capital gains tax on equities, and probable changes in taxation would come in the Union Budget for 2027-28, a senior official said on Monday.\nCentral Board of Direct Taxes (CBDT) Chairman Ravi Agrawal said the ministry is considering suggestions from various stakeholders made during the pre-budget meetings.\n\"We will consider it, and I'm sure on February 1 you will get to know. Analysis is being done of whatever issues have been flagged or points that have been raised by the stakeholders,\" Agrawal told reporters on the sidelines of the inauguration of a CBDT lounge at the IITF here.\nAgrawal said the different facets of the capital gains tax regime, including tax implications, will be examined, and the decision will be announced in the Budget.\nIndustry chambers have already made representations to the Ministry recommending abolition of Long Term Capital Gains tax (LTCG).\nThey also suggested rationalising short-term capital gains .",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-16T10:25:34"
    }
